questions.question:
(a) Suppose $\mathbb{R}$ be the set of all real numbers and $f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ is a function such that the following equations hold for all $x,y\in\mathbb{R}$: (i) $f(x+y)=f(x)+f(y)$;
(ii) $f(xy)=f(x)f(y)$. Show that for all $x\in\mathbb{R}$ either $f(x)=0$, or $f(x)=x$.
(b) Find the Laurent series which represent the function $\frac{1}{(1+z^{2})(z+2)}$ when (i) $|z|<1$;
(ii) $1<|z|<2$;
(iii) $|z|>2$.
(c) In a factory there are five operators $O_{1},O_{2},O_{3},O_{4},O_{5}$ and five machines $M_{1},M_{2},M_{3},M_{4},M_{5}$. The operating costs are given when the $O_{i}$ operator operates the $M_{j}$ machine ($i,j=1, 2,\ldots,5$). But there is a restriction that $O_{3}$ cannot be allowed to operate the third machine $M_{3}$ and $O_{2}$ cannot be allowed to operate the fifth machine $M_{5}$. The cost matrix (rows $O_{1}$ to $O_{5}$, columns $M_{1}$ to $M_{5}$) is $\begin{pmatrix}24&29&18&32&19\\17&26&34&22&21\\27&16&28&17&25\\22&18&28&30&24\\28&16&31&24&27\end{pmatrix}$. Find the optimal assignment and the optimal assignment cost also.

(a) Find the general solution of the partial differential equation $(y^{3}x-2x^{4})p+(2y^{4}-x^{3}y)q=9z(x^{3}-y^{3})$, where $p=\frac{\partial z}{\partial x}$, $q=\frac{\partial z}{\partial y}$, and find its integral surface that passes through the curve $x=t$, $y=t^{2}$, $z=1$.
(b) Find the equivalent of numbers given in a specified number system to the system mentioned against them: (i) $(111011\cdot 101)_{2}$ to decimal system;
(ii) $(1000111110000\cdot 00101100)_{2}$ to hexadecimal system;
(iii) $(\mathrm{C4F2})_{16}$ to decimal system;
(iv) $(418)_{10}$ to binary system.
(c) Suppose the Lagrangian of a mechanical system is given by $L=\frac{1}{2}m(a\dot{x}^{2}+2b\dot{x}\dot{y}+c\dot{y}^{2})-\frac{1}{2}k(ax^{2}+2bxy+cy^{2})$, where $a,b,c$, $m(>0)$, $k(>0)$ are constants and $b^{2}\ne ac$. Write down the Lagrangian equations of motion and identify the system.
